This file disables Jekyll processing on GitHub Pages.

Without it GitHub runs the published output through Jekyll, which silently
ignores every file and directory whose name starts with an underscore. Astro
emits all of its hashed JavaScript and CSS into `_astro/`, so the entire site
would load as unstyled HTML with no scripts and no obvious error anywhere.

The file has to exist in the published output, which is why it lives in
public/ rather than at the project root.
